  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "In regards to the new \"age assurance\" system some question and issue came up\n\nEven with the \"age assurance\" tag on a users profile please somewhere expose which version of verification they have used , some users might not trust a \"age estimation\" approach when wanting to make friends of the same age , users should have a right to see if a user is \"Maybe 18+\" or \"Id verified 18+\" , age estimation works and is a good thing to implement IF tools are being provided to be able to clearly differentiate between the two , a full \"merge\" to \"Age assurance\" will honestly create way more confusion between people as now they definitely wouldn't be able to trust a badge saying they are \"probably an adult\" \n\nLike i said estimation is a good thing for convenience of the user and data privacy , but we need to be able to differentiate between what system/s got used , this an easily accesible way to see the information within vrchat itself and on the website\n\nI understand why the two would want to be merged into \"Age Assurance\" umbrella term , but like i stated above i do think this will result in confusion between users and will result in way more issues than it solves",
